\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Sample definitions on the sky: two Lim--Tempel groups hosting embedded compact groups, in projected physical coordinates relative to the host BGG (east to the left, common scale); disc area is proportional to $r$-band luminosity. Black circles mark the CG\textsubscript  {4}{} members, blue squares the four brightest eligible members (the Control\textsubscript  {4B}{} quartet), and orange triangles the BGG and its three nearest eligible projected companions (the Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} quartet); the right-hand panels enlarge the boxed $\pm 170$~kpc windows. \textit  {(a)} CG\textsubscript  {4}{}~204 is an exact four-member Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} core of Lim group 1117. Across the 56 non-isolated systems, 51 have any projected-core overlap and 46 are exact identities; the remainder include partial and zero overlap (Appendix~\ref {app:cg_core_overlap}). \textit  {(b)} CG\textsubscript  {4}{}~330 is an off-centre substructure 670~kpc from the BGG of Lim group 1289: the Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} quartet contains no compact-group galaxy and is retained, whereas the Control\textsubscript  {4B}{} quartet contains the brightest CG\textsubscript  {4}{} member and is excluded.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{3}{Sample definitions on the sky: two Lim--Tempel groups hosting embedded compact groups, in projected physical coordinates relative to the host BGG (east to the left, common scale); disc area is proportional to $r$-band luminosity. Black circles mark the \CG {} members, blue squares the four brightest eligible members (the \CB {} quartet), and orange triangles the BGG and its three nearest eligible projected companions (the \CC {} quartet); the right-hand panels enlarge the boxed $\pm 170$~kpc windows. \textit {(a)} \CG {}~204 is an exact four-member \CC {} core of Lim group 1117. Across the 56 non-isolated systems, 51 have any projected-core overlap and 46 are exact identities; the remainder include partial and zero overlap (Appendix~\ref {app:cg_core_overlap}). \textit {(b)} \CG {}~330 is an off-centre substructure 670~kpc from the BGG of Lim group 1289: the \CC {} quartet contains no compact-group galaxy and is retained, whereas the \CB {} quartet contains the brightest \CG {} member and is excluded}{figure.1}{}}
