\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Satellite morphology versus median projected pair separation, \(\langle R_{ij}\rangle \), in physical kpc. \textit  {(a)} Upper panel: quartet separation distributions. Lower panel: E-class fractions among E/S-classified satellites at fixed \(\log (M_\star /\mathrm  {M}_\odot )=10.35\), in 0.2-dex separation bins, with 95\% intervals. Curves are sample-specific logistic fits in stellar mass and \(\log \langle R_{ij}\rangle \), evaluated at the same mass over each sample's central 90\% range. Grey shading marks the CG\textsubscript  {4}{}--Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} common range, 94--219~kpc. \textit  {(b)} CG\textsubscript  {4}{} minus Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} E-class fraction from the separate-slope model, evaluated over the covariate distribution of CG\textsubscript  {4}{} satellites in the same separation range; shading gives the pointwise 95\% interval. Symbols to the right of the divider summarise distinct comparisons at categorical positions: full-sample adjusted contrast (circle), compactness-matched quartets (square), and a match allowing a difference of at most \(120\,\mathrm  {km\,s}^{-1}\) in velocity dispersion (diamond). Bars are 95\% intervals. The raw-fraction version appears in the online supplement.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:compactness}{{3}{7}{Satellite morphology versus median projected pair separation, \(\Rmed \), in physical kpc. \textit {(a)} Upper panel: quartet separation distributions. Lower panel: E-class fractions among E/S-classified satellites at fixed \(\log (M_\star /\msun )=10.35\), in 0.2-dex separation bins, with 95\% intervals. Curves are sample-specific logistic fits in stellar mass and \(\log \Rmed \), evaluated at the same mass over each sample's central 90\% range. Grey shading marks the \CG {}--\CC {} common range, 94--219~kpc. \textit {(b)} \CG {} minus \CC {} E-class fraction from the separate-slope model, evaluated over the covariate distribution of \CG {} satellites in the same separation range; shading gives the pointwise 95\% interval. Symbols to the right of the divider summarise distinct comparisons at categorical positions: full-sample adjusted contrast (circle), compactness-matched quartets (square), and a match allowing a difference of at most \(120\kms \) in velocity dispersion (diamond). Bars are 95\% intervals. The raw-fraction version appears in the online supplement}{figure.3}{}}
